## Install your client

<CodeTabs examples={{TypeScript:'npm install @miosa/sdk',Python:'pip install miosa'}} />

The installation and cloud examples are reference snippets. This documentation does not execute them or require an API key to read them.

## Create a client

Keep the credential in the server environment. Create a client where the application can reuse its configuration rather than scattering keys through handlers.

<CodeTabs examples={{TypeScript:'import { Miosa } from "@miosa/sdk";\n\nconst miosa = new Miosa({\n  apiKey: \"YOUR_API_KEY\",\n});',Python:'from miosa import Miosa\n\nclient = Miosa(\n    api_key="YOUR_API_KEY",\n)'}} />

## Keep the returned identity

An SDK makes a request easier to express; it does not remove the need to inspect its result. Keep the resource identifier and state returned by a create operation. Use that exact identifier in later requests.

## Handle the operation you started

For a long-running operation, preserve its identity and inspect its state. A timeout in the calling process is not evidence that nothing happened on the server.

## Explore the local contract

The [API explorer](/docs/api) provides working requests against this reconstruction’s local example API. Its schema describes that example surface rather than claiming full compatibility with the production SDK.
